              "note_id": "CON_0001",
              "exact_quote": "Two exchange rates are shown, one quoted as euro‑dollar and the other quoted opposite to the usual market convention."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0002",
              "exact_quote": "When the exchange rate goes up, it means an appreciation of the local currency (the dollar)."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0003",
              "exact_quote": "When the exchange rate goes down, it indicates a depreciation of the local currency."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0023",
              "exact_quote": "the dollar becomes more expensive (appreciation) when the domestic interest rate rises"
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0024",
              "exact_quote": "the relationship linking interest rate differentials to expected changes in exchange rates"
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0036",
              "exact_quote": "In equilibrium you have to be indifferent; exchange rate moves until indifference is restored."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0037",
              "exact_quote": "Exchange rate and interest rate have a positive relationship; as one rises, the other rises."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0045",
              "exact_quote": "You can determine the exchange rate by plotting and using the interest rate through UIP."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0046",
              "exact_quote": "The interest rate is used together with UIP to find the exchange rate."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0047",
              "exact_quote": "UIP provides a point that links the interest rate to the exchange rate."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "CON_0005",
              "exact_quote": "The policy itself concerns the exchange rate and can affect output and the interest rate."
            },
            {
              "note_id": "FCT_0083",
              "exact_quote": "The interest rate is set by the Fed, not by the ECB."
            },
            {
